# Fixed 2026-10-07, defect 458, lane b14-check: the shape beside it with
# the `@` left off. Symptom: `end_lease(c)` on a lease cell was told *this
# argument is not such a cell*, where `c` is one and the mistake is the
# missing `@`. Now it is told the `@` it owes, as a call to any function that
# changes its argument is, with the certain fix that writes it.

function main()
    x = "abc"
    c: cstr @= x.lease()
    end_lease(@c)  #~ marker_mismatch
